Mini Project Assignment: 
Employee Payroll System

Objective
Build a system where:
Employees have personal details


Salary is protected (hidden properly)


Bonus is calculated using global policy


Company details are shared


Internal logic is controlled

---

Step 1: Create Global Variable
 Requirement:
Create a global variable:

bonus_percentage = 12

---
Step 2: Create Class 
Employee

🔹 Add Class Variable
 Requirement:
company_name = "InfotechLabs"


🔹 Constructor (__init__)
 Take parameters:
name
salary
currency

 Store as:
name → public
__salary → private
_currency → protected


---

 
Step 3: Add Methods

1️⃣ Public Method → 
show_details()
 Should print:
name
company
currency
 Do NOT print salary directly

2️⃣ Private Method → 
__calculate_bonus()
 Logic:
Calculate bonus using global variable
Return bonus value

3️⃣ Public Method → 
generate_salary()
 Should:
Call private method
Create local variable final_salary
Print final salary with currency

4️⃣ Protected Method → 
_convert_currency()
 Just print:
“Currency conversion happening”
 Call this method inside generate_salary()
---

 Step 4: Inheritance
Create a child class:
class Manager(Employee):

Override Method
 Override show_details()
Call parent method using super()

Add:
print("Role: Manager")
---

 Step 5: Object Creation
Create:
e1 = Employee("Shivam", 50000, "INR")
e2 = Manager("Rahul", 80000, "USD")

 Call Methods
e1.show_details()
e1.generate_salary()

e2.show_details()
e2.generate_salary()
---

 Step 6: Testing (IMPORTANT)
Try these and observe:
print(e1.name)        # ✅ Should work
print(e1._currency)   # ⚠️ Should work (but not recommended)
print(e1.__salary)    # ❌ Should fail
print(e1._Employee__salary)  # ⚠️ Name mangling


 Expected Learning
After this assignment, students should understand:
✔ Why private variables are used
✔ Why protected is just a convention
✔ How global variable affects all objects
✔ Difference between class vs instance variable
✔ Use of local variable in calculation
✔ Real use of inheritance

---
 Bonus Challenge (For Smart Students)
 Add:
Setter method to update salary safely
Validation: salary should not be negative



